    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0320" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2616</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1916, noon</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 9, 8 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. General blockade of Greek ports has been commenced by the French. No notice
                    given to Greek Government and legations here deny all knowledge.</p>
                <p>Presume that purpose is to force government to resign and to procure formation of
                    a new government after election, but the greatest uncertainty prevails here as
                    to purpose and scope of blockade.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Droppers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
